<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111960" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινικ-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>red</i> or <i>purple cloth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				731
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				735
			</span></i>; used for horses, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.3.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>red cloak,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				320
			</span></i> (troch.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινικίδ᾽ ὀξεῖαν
			πάνυ</span> a <i>red cloak</i> as bright as bright can be,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1173
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1175
			</span></i> (both troch.): esp. the <i>dark-red military cloak</i> of
			the Lacedaemonians, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				1140
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Lac.</u>
				11.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				542
			</span></i>; also worn by Persians, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.4.1
			</span></i>, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινικιστής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			; by Macedonians, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Aem.</u>
				18
			</span></i>, etc.; distd. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πορφυρίς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.3.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>red curtain</i> or <i>carpet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.76
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>red flag</i> hung out as the signal for action, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.66.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				13.77
			</span></i>, etc.; generally, <i>red banner,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φοινικίδας ἀνασείειν,</span> a form in
			solemn curses or excommunications, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.51
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>ornamental palm-tree, Inscr. Délos</i><i><span class="en">
				314
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				137
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
